[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Settled architecture lives in a .sdoc directory beside the code

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION
TITLE: Settled architecture lives in a .sdoc directory beside the code
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: >>>
A source-comment extractor exists, at which point these nodes either move into
the source files they describe or stay put and the extractor feeds them.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
Architecture nodes that describe a specific package live in a .sdoc directory
next to that package, not under docs/plans. Each node names the source file it
describes with a File relation. Line anchors are recorded in prose until an
extractor can carry them.

The competing option, deferred: keep every node under docs/ and rely on general
source extractors to associate them with code. That option needs the extractor
to exist first, so it cannot be chosen today.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Colocation works with no tooling. Plans decay and are collected; settled
architecture about a package should outlive the plan that produced it and should
move with the package if it moves.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Human acceptance needed. Both options are live and the choice is reversible: the
nodes carry global UIDs, so relocating them changes no edge.
<<<
